 * Barriers" conversion + SEO / AEO / GEO product page.
 *
 * Bespoke page (not the YAML-driven generic ProductPage), built to mirror the
 * structure, class helpers and progressive-enhancement motion of the sibling
 * spokes src/pages/gym-flooring-rolls/zainduo.astro,
 * src/pages/rubber-gym-tiles/zainfit.astro and
 * src/pages/rubber-gym-tiles/zainsquare.astro, and the parent hub
 * src/pages/gym-safety-accessories.astro.
 *
 * ─── ROUTING ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * The content entry src/content/products/curb-stone.yaml still carries
 * `path: /gym-safety-accessories/curb-stone` (a child of the `gym` hub). To
 * avoid a duplicate-route build error the matching branch is filtered out of
 * getStaticPaths in src/pages/[...slug].astro — the same pattern already used
 * for zainfit, zainsquare, zainduo and zainactive-rolls. The YAML entry stays
 * as data; this file serves the URL.
 *
 * ─── STACK DEVIATION FROM THE BUILD REQUEST ─────────────────────────────
 * The request named React / Next.js (App Router) + lucide-react. This project
 * is a static Astro site (output: 'static', zero-JS by default, no
 * @astrojs/react) deployed to Netlify — see CLAUDE.md. To keep the page
 * zero-JS and consistent with every sibling spoke:
 *   - Icons: the SAME Lucide glyphs are inlined below as 24×24 stroke path
 *     data — identical rendered output, no client runtime.
 *   - "App Router metadata" → Astro <head> metadata via BaseLayout/Seo props.
 *   - The BreadcrumbList schema from the request is emitted (host normalised to
 *     the configured canonical domain — see CANONICAL HOST note) together with
 *     Product + FAQPage in one combined @graph, matching the sibling spokes and
 *     CLAUDE.md §5.
 *
 * ─── CANONICAL HOST ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * The request shows "rukanalzain.com"; the configured site is
 * "ruknalzain.ae" (astro.config.mjs). Canonical + schema URLs are built
 * from the configured host via the BaseLayout `canonical` prop — same choice as
 * the zainduo / zainsquare siblings. trailingSlash: 'never' (astro.config.mjs),
 * so no trailing slashes on internal item URLs.
 *
 * ─── IMAGE ASSETS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Client-supplied JPEGs in public/images/gym-safety-accessories/, wired below
 * with intrinsic width/height to prevent layout shift:
 *   - zain-curb-stone-hero.jpg                        (hero)
 *   - zain-curb-stone-dramatic-shatter-impact.jpg     (problem/solution)
 *   - zain-curb-stone-mirror-protection-closeup.jpg   (applications)
 * TODO: convert these to optimised WebP to match the parent hub's asset
 * pipeline (its set is WebP; the JPEG sources there were deleted post-convert).
 * og:image falls back to the hero file (no purpose-built 1200×630 card yet).
 *
 * ─── DATA INTEGRITY FLAGS (CLAUDE.md §0 + §6) ───────────────────────────
 *   - The §5 technical table is DESCRIPTIVE only (composition, protection
 *     scope, thermal / chemical behaviour, install method) — verbatim from the
 *     request, no numbers asserted. curb-stone.yaml still lists Dimensions
 *     (L×W×H), Weight and Colour options as unfilled TODOs; collect and publish
 *     those before go-live.
 *   - Hero primary CTA scrolls to the in-page lead-capture form (#lead-form),
 *     a Netlify Forms POST — matching contact.astro and the sibling spokes.
 *   - FAQ answers are reused verbatim from the parent hub
 *     (src/pages/gym-safety-accessories.astro) so terminology stays consistent
 *     across the hub and spoke (CLAUDE.md §3).
 */
